Z||000000||fieroboy||07-02-2000||11:30 AM||||how do i remove the window crank to remove the door panel ???? ||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||07-02-2000||11:32 AM||||It's held by a clip under it. you need a tool to remove the clip. you can get the tool at any parts store or even sears I think. don't even try to remove the clip w/o the tool. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||07-02-2000||02:42 PM||||Actually, I used a couple of small, flat bladed screwdrivers the 1st time and the "Christmas tree" removal tool the second time.  Not as easy as using the correct tool, but possible.<P>------------------<BR>Dave-<BR>Grape Ape ('85GT)||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fret Naught||07-03-2000||01:37 AM||||I used a button hook for years, a trick my dad tought me. but it just so happens I had my door handels off a couple of days ago and while I had them off I made a tool, took about five min. get a piece of sheet metal about 18 gauge I would guess, cut a rectangular piece 12" long and 1-1.25" wide. In one end cut a slot 1/2" wide and about 1" long knock off the sharp edges with a file and bingo you have your own special tool. Actually, the slot should be just a skosh over 1/2" wide.<BR>Have fun||||reg||1
